  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The Lewis dot structure of the given molecules will be the following.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c2022a3a-0304-4cfc-9f90-e7f14a59d21c-fd85c6e5-359d-4c7b-a316-7f1122860d89-image.png\" style=\"width: 372px; height: 366px;\" /></p><p>As we can see in above structures that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>lone</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bond</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>one</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>lone</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>two</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bond</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>two</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>lone</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bond</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>lone</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bond</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pair</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
